Input: {"question": "What sport is Scott Jackson associated with?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d00", "start": 0, "end": 181, "text": "Scott Jackson (American football) Scott Jackson (born January 19, 1979) is a former American football offensive lineman for the Houston Texans of the National Football League (NFL)."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d00", "start": 182, "end": 327, "text": "He was originally signed by the Tampa Bay Buccaneers as an undrafted free agent in 2004 and ended his five-year NFL career on the Houston Texans."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d00", "start": 328, "end": 383, "text": "He played college football at Brigham Young University."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d00", "start": 384, "end": 497, "text": "Jackson was a star offensive lineman for Palos Verdes Peninsula High School in Rolling Hills Estates, California."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d00", "start": 498, "end": 617, "text": "A three-year letterwinner, Jackson was named all-west, all-state and Los Angeles Times Lineman of the Year as a senior."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d00", "start": 618, "end": 635, "text": "He graduated from"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d01", "start": 0, "end": 232, "text": "American football - Wikipedia Home Random Nearby Log in Settings Donate About Wikipedia Disclaimers Search American football Article Talk Language Watch View source This article is about the American variation of gridiron football ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d01", "start": 233, "end": 292, "text": "For other uses , see American football ( disambiguation ) ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0114-0f870c2425aa:d01", "start":